		{
			dependencies: ["09B4D23146EF5CC0"]
			description: [
				"&6&l\"Adaptive power grid system terminal\""
				"&9is the core control block of the adaptive power grid system, managing the voltage levels of the entire base's energy warehouse with one click."
				""
				"&7▌ Tutorial:"
				"&l1. Place the terminal of the adaptive distribution network system first"
				""
				"&l2. Click Permission Control in the lower left corner of the GUI. Click on the interface that displays English. The owner of the main interface will be displayed as your ID."
				""
				"&l3. Click Frequency Settings in the lower left corner of the GUI and adjust the frequency to 1"
				""
				"&lAt this point, the setting of the adaptive distribution grid system terminal is completed."
				""
				"&7▌ Suggestions:"
				"&l&6You can also control the configuration without changing the permissions, and the power grid will support everyone’s use."
			]
			id: "63CF08FB993E876A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4D339BA584DE754F"
				item: "gtmadvancedhatch:adaptive_net_energy_terminal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -16.5d
			y: 23.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["09B4D23146EF5CC0"]
			description: [
				"&6&l「 Adaptive power grid warehouse / Adaptive power grid laser warehouse 」"
				"&9can follow the terminal configuration to automatically synchronize the voltage level of the smart warehouse, achieving synchronization at one end and taking effect throughout the base."
				""
				"&7▌ Function:"
				"After&lis placed, you can use the&6network configuration flash memory&7to right-click to bind, or the secondary handheld flash memory is automatically bound to the network when it is placed."
				"When&lremains loaded with the terminal, the voltage configuration level is automatically synchronized every second by default."
				""
				"&7▌ Suggestions:"
				"&l&6When the machine is running, if the power level of the warehouse is reduced synchronously, it may cause the operation to be suspended. It needs to be synchronized back to a sufficient level to continue."
			]
