		{
			dependencies: ["639BE904FFDCED52"]
			description: [
				"&9&lGTLAdditions「Planetary Ionization Combined Tower」"
				""
				"&7▌ Function:"
				"&lcan only use coils of Titan steel and above."
				"&lEvery 3 seconds is a working cycle."
				"&lIf there is still energy entering after the internal energy buffer is full, an extremely large explosion will occur centered on the machine."
				"At the beginning of the&lcycle, a 1-tick instantaneous extremely high-power EU pulse is generated to charge the cache, and the remaining time is smoothly discharged at lower power."
				"After the&lpulse ends, the cache will output power through the power compartment or laser source compartment."
				""
				"&lThe level of the stellar thermal container affects the cache amount:"
				"&l• Base: 54.12 trillion EU"
				"&l• Advanced: 3475 trillion EU"
				"&l• Ultimate: 1160 trillion EU"
				""
				"&lcoil level affects the type of fluid consumed, consumption per cycle and power generation:"
				""
				"&l• Titansteel ~ Adamantite: consumes 73728 mB of liquid iron, 8 KB of liquid ice, and 0.0002 space drone MKII"
				"&linstantaneous maximum 4096 A, discharge maximum 16 A"
				"&l• Super Silica ~ Starlight: consumes 36864 mB of liquid tantalum, 4 KB of liquid helium, and 0.0001 space drone MKIV"
				"&linstantaneous maximum 524288 A, discharge maximum 256 A"
				"&l• Endless ~ Eternity: consumes Liquid Crystal Matrix 9216 mB, Extremely Cold Ice 1 KB, Space Drone MKVI 0.000025 pieces"
				"&linstantaneous maximum 268435456 A, discharge maximum 131072 A"
				""
				"&7▌ Note:"
				"&l&6The machine mechanism is more complex. For more detailed instructions, please refer to the GTLAdditions guide."
			]
			id: "6A290776C446E304"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3E65FA19873023AA"
				item: "gtladditions:planetary_ionisation_convergence_tower"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 4.5d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["69799F6DE604C84B"]
			description: [
				"&9&lGTLAdditions「Time Warper」"
				""
				"&7▌ Function:"
				"&lIt is the binding gain machine of the final zigzag quantum wave matrix."
				"&lFirst use the hyperspace data module to right-click the Final Zigzag Quantum Wave Matrix to record the data, and then right-click the space-time warper to complete the binding."
				"&lThe time and space warper itself needs to run the No. 1 circuit idling recipe, which consumesOpVenergy and takes 30 seconds."
				"After the&lFinal Zigzag Quantum Fluctuation Matrix completes the current round of actual parallel consumption, it will count the total number of successfully processed parallels and try to consume gain resources from the bound space-time warper. All resources are first inspected as a whole and then deducted after passing them."
				"After the&lgain resource is successfully consumed, only the recipe output of this round will be amplified, and the probability input, probability output or parallel calculation method will not be changed."
				""
				"&lcausal distortion level (output multiplier and additional consumption):"
				""
				"&l• Level 1: Multiplier 1.3 times, additional consumption of Liquid Endless, quantity = total parallel ÷ 17"
				"&l• Level 2: Multiply 1.7 times, consume additional liquid Hypergen on the basis of level 1, quantity = total parallel ÷ 28"
				"&l• Level 3: Multiply 2.6 times, consume additional liquid space-time based on level 2, quantity = total parallelism ÷ 44"
				"&l• Level 4: 3.2x multiplier, additional consumption of Quantum Anomalies (Number = Total Parallelism ÷ 730) and Hypercubes (Number = Total Parallelism ÷ 873) over Level 3"
				""
				"&lquantity calculation uses integer division, and this item is not consumed when the result is 0."
			]
			id: "71C998A12CC2E315"
			min_width: 250
			tasks: [{
				id: "1489D7C96AAEF51C"
				item: "gtladditions:time_space_distorter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 22.5d
			y: 20.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["69799F6DE604C84B"]
			description: [
				"&9&lGTLAdditions「Recursive inversion array」"
				""
				"&7▌ Function:"
				"&lIt is not an independent production machine, but is bound to a formed furnace of false gods. It reads the status of its own formed modules and provides gains for the bound host."
				""
				"&luses the overtime data module for binding:"
				"&l• First right-click on the formed Furnace of False Gods and record the binding source."
				"&l• Right-click the formed recursive inversion array in the same dimension to establish binding."
				"&l• The new binding will overwrite the old binding on both machines."
				"&l• In survival mode, the data module will be consumed after successful binding; in creative mode, only the record will be cleared."
				"&l• Right-click on Sneak to clear the saved records."
				"&l• Cross-dimensional bindings will be rejected."
				""
				"&lRecursive Inversion Gain Pack Requirements: The False God's Forge is formed, the array is formed, and the connected Chrono Boost Engine is running and not overheating. Then make a probability judgment based on the perfect space-time boost parameters:"
				"&l• When the temperature is 93000K–97000K, the parameter is 1.0, and the gain package must take effect."
				"&l• When the temperature is outside this range and the parameter is less than 1.0, the gain package takes effect based on probability."
				""
				"&lWhen the gain probability determination fails, the output/EU gain of the catalytic selection array, the magnetic current convergence core focus, the space-time stasis device, and the hyperspace boost engine EU reduction will not take effect. The basic output multiplier and EU reduction based on running time of the bound host itself still take effect normally. The Star Ceremony entrance is separate from this probability determination: it strictly requires that the booster engines are running, not overheated, and at 93000K–97000K."
				""
				"&lEach module must be installed in the array module location or connected in parallel to the array. The module interrupts its own operation when not connected."
			]
			id: "4F11EC28E969297C"
			min_width: 250
			tasks: [{
				id: "6C24D3A0C0C185AC"
				item: "gtladditions:recursive_reverse_array"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 22.5d
			y: 22.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["69799F6DE604C84B"]
			description: [
				"&9&lrecursive inversion array · module"
				""
				"&7▌ Function:"
				"&lFirst form the Forge of the False God and the recursive inversion array, and bind them with the hyperspace data module (same dimension, survival mode consumes modules). The array needs to connect all modules to take effect."
				""
				"&7▌ Catalytic selection array"
				"&l• There is a cycle every 32 seconds, and the redstone signal (1-15) is output at 0 seconds to tell you which catalyst is needed for this round (1-3 crude, 4-6 ordinary, 7-9 radiant, 10-12 alien, 13-15 stellar)."
				"&l• Check the LV giant fluid input bin every second starting from the 7th second, and the correct catalyst consumption is 40B/s → output magnification × 2, EU magnification + 0.15."
				"&l• Wrong input or no catalyst → Lost output gain (EU gain may remain partially)."
				""
				"&7▌ Magnetic flow convergence core"
				"&l• Only focus on the fluid output, merge multiple outputs into the first one, and then multiply the magnification (less than 2 outputs will be invalid)."
				"&l• 12-second fuel cycle, randomly select 2 types of item requirements (super-solid super-energy silica blackbody/quantum anomaly/super-stable self-healing adhesive, 1-16384 each) and 1 fluid requirement."
				"&l• Activation conditions: Accurately input items through 2 ULV giant item buses, input fluid into 1 LV giant fluid tank, and continuously supply 2 magnetic material blocks/second. If satisfied, focus is enabled."
				""
				"&7▌ Space-time stasis device"
				"&l• 0pV continuous operation, consuming 70B/s liquid space-time."
				"&l• Running by itself + public gain gate on → the running time will not be lost when the bound host is idle (no active increase, just a minimum)."
				""
				"&7▌ Hypertime boost engine"
				"&l• UXV runs continuously and is a necessary module for common gain gating."
				"&l• Temperature control: initial 48000K, optimal range 93000K-97000K, overheating threshold 105000K."
				"&l• +1300K/s when working and -900K/s when idle. Temperature control fluid 100B/s: heating (lava +2500, liquid flame +4600, primitive star mixture +14000); cooling (liquid ice -1900, liquid ammonia -3400, extreme cold ice -6700)."
				"&l• Stops providing gate control after overheating, and the cooling rate becomes -7125K/s until it returns to 48000K."
				"&l• Installing the Vientiane Transcription node can output the redstone value corresponding to the current temperature."
				""
				"&7▌ Note:"
				"&l• Validity judgment of recursive inversion gain package: When the temperature is 93000K-97000K, the perfect parameter is 1.0, which will definitely take effect; outside the interval, it will take effect according to the parameter probability. If the probability fails, all recursive inversion module gains (catalytic output/EU, magnetic flow focusing, stagnation, engine EU reduction) will be invalid, but the basic multiplier of the host itself will still be there."
				"&l• The Star Ceremony entrance does not rely on this probability, it requires the engine to be running, not overheated, and at 93000-97000K."
				"&l• Each module must be installed at the module position of the array or connected in parallel. The module interrupts operation when not connected."
			]
			id: "2DA56B0E68E80FC0"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "5AD710A60C98F84D"
					item: "gtladditions:catalytic_cascade_array"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "164AB562454859F7"
					item: "gtladditions:magnetorheological_convergence_core"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "5E77B9F15834D8D9"
					item: "gtladditions:spacetime_stasis_device"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "061443694B28FD3B"
					item: "gtladditions:supratemporal_boosting_engine"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Recursive inversion array · module"
			x: 22.5d
			y: 24.75d
		}
